                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                        "entry_id": "7c27e573-319b-3956-a67c-b91136bb2d70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or characteristic of being indescribable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b52fcce-65ce-4c14-9b08-00ab833423be",
                                "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                                "text": "Sensorial changes are by no means uncommon, and they are of every kind, description, and indescribability."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1ef90ea-4bc5-4d22-affa-fae687f35c09",
                                "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                                "text": "These ideas may seem at first sight somewhat startling; but when we realise the extraordinary depth and indescribability of the emotions of music, the very remoteness and far-reachingness of the explanation is in favour of its validity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dcfe2f60-9975-4dff-9535-3c73095f0305",
                                "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                                "text": "This perception, if we look to its origin, may turn out to be primitive; no doubt the feeling of \"crude extensity\" is an original sensation; every inference, association, and distinction is a thing that looms up suddenly before the mind, and the nature and actuality of which is a datum of what — to indicate its irresistible immediacy and indescribability — we may well call sense. Forms are seen, and if we think of the origin of the perception, we may well call this vision a sensation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b93b91d-3ee2-47d0-9ba8-24300b1960fe",
                                "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                                "text": "But the unembodied Justice, whereof that other is either an emblem, or else is a fearful indescribability, is not so visible!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a06ff1a7-9cb7-4b07-bb32-38efae630c97",
                                "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                                "text": "The featurelessness of the affective quality, on the other hand, its indescribability, is due to the very simplicity of its relation to the organism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b44ab9c6-37f2-4117-adef-9f46db575256",
                                "sense_id": "d4adb169-8791-31ea-b900-1c93067ef1df",
                                "text": "This emphasis on the indescribability of God in intense religious experience is consistently found in the more mystical religious traditions."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12781a7e-f5bf-31e4-a17c-27fc1145b184",
                        "entry_id": "7c27e573-319b-3956-a67c-b91136bb2d70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something which cannot be described."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8d113fe-a964-4e7d-bd59-2e7f17a9ca10",
                                "sense_id": "12781a7e-f5bf-31e4-a17c-27fc1145b184",
                                "text": "The clothed embodied justice that sits in Westminster Hall, with penalties, parchments, tipstaves, is very visible. But the unembodied justice, whereof that other is either an emblem, or else is a fearful indescribability, is not so visible!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
